# UNIX terminal commands

## Changing current working directory

- Go up one dir

```bash
cd ..
```

- Go up two dir

```bash
cd ../..
```

- Go up to inside dir

```bash
cd [directory]
```

- Go to root dir

```bash
cd /
```

- Go to previous dir

```bash
cd -
```

- Go to home dir

```bash
cd ~
```

or

```bash
cd
```

- Absolute path

```bash
cd /Users/nursultanlukmanov/documents/auca
```

## Go to some existing directory and create a new directory

```bash
cd lab-1
mkdir my_dir
```

or

```bash
mkdir lab-1/mydir
```

## Create a file

```bash
touch file-1.txt
```

## Grant all the permission to file

```bash
chmod 777 file-1.txt
```

## Read file

- All content

```bash
cat small-file.txt
```

- With scrolling (Best for larger files)

```bash
less huge-file.txt.txt
```

## Copy file

- Copy to file

```bash
cp source.txt destination.txt
```

```bash
cp huge-file.txt small-file.txt
```

- Copy to a directory

```bash
cp huge-file.txt dir-1/backup/
```

- Copy multiple files into a directory

```bash
cp huge-file.txt small-file dir-1/backup/
```

## copy directories

```bash
cp -r dir-1/backup dir-2/backup
```

## Delete file or folder

### Delete a file

```bash
rm dir-2/backup/huge-file.txt
```

### Delete a folder and its content


```bash
rm dir-2/backup
```

## Task 

### Create two directories and move all files instead of copying from one directory to another

```bash 
mv dir-1/backup dir-2/backup
```

